# sid:1 and sid:2 each unset the bit the other checks with isnotset. The graph
# gets an unset -> isnotset edge in both directions, which forms a cycle.
#
# isnotset already matches before a bit was ever set, so neither rule has to
# wait for the other and both can match on the first packet of a flow. The
# cycle is not a real dependency and must not be reported.
alert tcp any any -> any any (flowbits:isnotset,A; flowbits:unset,B; sid:1;)
alert tcp any any -> any any (flowbits:isnotset,B; flowbits:unset,A; sid:2;)
